---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { contact, ownerSupplied } from "../data/site";

const description =
  "Privacy notice for Straight Up Digital, describing the personal information collected through the website, how it is used, and how to exercise your rights under POPIA.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description={description}
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <section class="legal">
        <div class="container legal__inner">
          <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
          <p class="legal__meta">Version 1.2 · Last updated 25 November 2026</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This notice explains what personal information Straight Up Digital
          collects through this website, why it is collected, who it is shared
          with and what you can ask us to do with it. It is written to be read,
          not to hide behind.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{ownerSupplied.legalEntity}</strong> operates from
          {contact.address}. Straight Up Digital is not
          described here as a registered company.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy questions and requests can be sent to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or through the{" "}
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
        <p>When you submit an enquiry or audit request, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your name, if you provide it.</li>
          <li>Your business name and website address.</li>
          <li>Your email address and, if you choose to provide it, your phone number.</li>
          <li>The service you are interested in and the message you write.</li>
          <li>The date and time you gave consent, and the version of this notice you agreed to.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The web host also records standard technical information such as the IP
          address, browser type and pages requested, in server logs used for
          security and troubleshooting.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not ask for identity numbers, card details, passwords or special
          personal information through this website. Please do not send them.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To read and respond to your enquiry.</li>
          <li>To prepare an audit, quote or proposal you have asked for.</li>
          <li>When the online report feature is enabled, to publish the reviewed customer report and receive your chosen next step or message.</li>
          <li>To deliver work you have agreed to and to keep the records the law requires.</li>
          <li>To keep the website secure and prevent abuse of the forms.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Under POPIA, we rely on your consent for the enquiry, on the steps needed
          to prepare or perform a contract, and on our legitimate interest in
          running a secure website. You can withdraw consent at any time by asking
          us to delete your enquiry.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell personal information. We share it only with service
          providers that help run the website and the business:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — website hosting, form-processing Worker
            and security controls. Cloudflare receives the form request and
            technical data such as an IP address and may process requests at its
            global edge locations, including outside South Africa.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Cloud Firestore</strong> — the accepted enquiry and
            private report records are stored in the production database region in
            Johannesburg, South Africa (<code>africa-south1</code>). The owner can
            retrieve an enquiry into the private local CRM; after successful
            import, the temporary Firestore queue copy is deleted. Rate-limit
            records are short-lived and are used to reduce form abuse.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Zoho Mail</strong> — receives enquiry notifications at
            straightupdigital@zohomail.com through the Zoho Mail API. The message
            includes the details you submit so the owner can respond. Zoho Mail for
            this account uses a United States data centre; mailbox copies are
            subject to Zoho's processing and retention practices.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Paystack</strong> — if a Paystack payment option is offered
            for an order, Paystack processes payment and transaction information
            to complete and manage that payment. Payment details are handled by
            Paystack; Straight Up Digital does not request or store your full
            card number or card security code in the website enquiry form. The
            payment provider's own privacy terms also apply to that transaction.
            Online checkout is not active on this website at the date of this
            notice.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The private local Business Auditor CRM</strong> — the owner may
            import enquiries from Firestore and runs the full audit on a private
            computer. The CRM and full audit are not served to website visitors.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Online customer reports</strong> — report publishing and client
            responses are currently disabled in production. If enabled, only the
            owner-reviewed customer-safe report would be stored in Johannesburg
            Firestore; its private link would expire after 30 days. A client's
            response would be emailed to the business inbox.
          </li>
          <li>
            Professional advisers or authorities, where the law requires it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Although enquiry and report records are stored in Johannesburg, Cloudflare
          and Zoho may process information outside South Africa. This can involve a
          cross-border transfer under POPIA. A South African database location on
          its own does not establish compliance; appropriate legal grounds and
          safeguards must apply to each transfer. Contact us if you need more
          information about a particular service provider or transfer.
        </p>

        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          A website enquiry stays in the private Firestore queue until the owner
          imports and acknowledges it; the queue copy is then deleted. The owner
          may retain the local CRM and Zoho mailbox copies as needed to respond,
          deliver agreed work and meet record-keeping obligations. No automatic
          deletion schedule is configured for those copies. Online report
          publishing is currently disabled; if enabled, report links and stored
          report records are scheduled to expire and be deleted after 30 days.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Cookies and analytics</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not set advertising or tracking cookies and does not use
          analytics. If that changes, this notice will be updated and consent will
          be requested where required by law.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under POPIA you may ask to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Be told what personal information we hold about you.</li>
          <li>Correct information that is wrong or out of date.</li>
          <li>Delete information we no longer have a lawful reason to keep.</li>
          <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
          <li>Withdraw consent for future processing.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Send the request through the <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a> and say
          what you want us to do. We may need to confirm your identity before
          acting. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to
          the Information Regulator (South Africa).
        </p>

        <h2>8. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Access to enquiries is limited to the people who need it to respond and
          deliver the work. The website is served over HTTPS, and form submissions
          are validated before they are accepted. No system is perfectly secure,
          but we take reasonable steps to protect what you send.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children</h2>
        <p>
          The website is intended for businesses and is not directed at children.
          We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          When this notice changes, the version date at the top changes too. If the
          change affects how consent works, the form will point to the new version
          before it is submitted.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For any privacy question, email{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or use the{" "}
          <a href="/contact">enquiry form</a> and mark the message “Privacy”.
          {ownerSupplied.informationOfficer} is the business's privacy contact.
        </p>
        <p>Business location: {contact.address}. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
